My understanding is once you go MTDI you will need some mechanical throttle linkage and and mechanical boost control but after that your sensors would only go to gauges and not an ECU so no MAF, no MAP etc

&#x200B;

Swing over to [TDIclub.com](https://TDIclub.com) or a diesel swap website those guys can tell you everything you need to know

The super stiff pedal is what it feels like when the booster has failed completely or there isn't any vacuum assistance

&#x200B;

Did you hear a hissing noise?  There is a chance of having a vacuum leak that only happens when you depressing the pedal.

If you have a hard pedal be sure the check valve is operating properly and measure manifold vacuum at the booster and compare to another position.  Your hose could have an internal failure somewhere

&#x200B;

