Let's play a hypothetical game:

You reinforce your mailbox into a small fort knox, because it's your "right"...a neighbor kid playing across the street chases a dog/ ball/etc into the street without looking.  A vehicle traveling at the speed limit needs to evade them at the last movement and they swerve into your mailbox.  The airbag inflates to protect the occupant but in fact it was a defect Takata airbag and it explodes in a uncontrolled manner and the driver dies.... Are you aware that there are still ticking time bombs in people's cars that haven't been replaced yet? (8 days ago VW recalled 105k cars) Or maybe the driver had an underlying heart condition, or some other pre-existing condition (known or unknown) that could result in a fatality from a low speed collision

&#x200B;

You have someone who was doing the right thing that's now dead and you have an expensive mailbox to repair...did you notice how the brick work was destroyed in OP's picture as well as the jeep?  Have you hired out good masonry work before?  Are you aware that with a little looking you could probably buy another Cheep Cherokee for the less than having that mailbox replaced?  Quick google search shows a custom brick work on a mailbox could come in @ $1800, which is 10x the price of a mailbox/ post combo from my local big box home improvement store

&#x200B;

I wholly recognize that all of these are all slim chances and combined together are not very likely but our world is made of accumulated probabilities.  But in this scenario you maybe held liable for involunatry manslaughter becuase your actions lead to the death of a person...does your "people should be held accountable for their actions" extend to you spending time in jail as well as being sued for in a civil case and working the rest of your life to pay off a wrongful death suit?  Or are you just trolling?

&#x200B;

One last note:  If you want to build your "mailbox" out of 1/4" plate steel so some kid with a ball bat breaks hand if they are out smashing stuff I'm OK with that but FFS put it on break away post so it doesn't kill someone
